  book_clue_index: 111
  content: This seems to be part of a mystery series. Maybe I should look for the
    earlier volumes.
  clue_content: "Near dawn, the woman laughed.\r\n\u201CThe man thinks going to sea
    will improve his mood.\u201D\r\n\u201CDoes it?\u201D\r\n\u201CI haven\u2019t
    got that far.\u201D\r\nShe asked Mara\u2019s name for the record. The line went
    dead before Mara could answer.\r\nAt home, Mara opened her copy of Moby-Dick.
    Beside the first sentence was a small coffee stain.\r\nMara packed it with her
    other novels. Inside she placed a notebook, a telephone number, and the words:\r\nAfter
    midnight. Ask her to stay."
